Use MAX_STATIC_DATA of 500000.
When play begins, seed the random-number generator with 1234.

container is a kind of thing.
door is a kind of thing.
object-like is a kind of thing.
supporter is a kind of thing.
food is a kind of object-like.
key is a kind of object-like.
containers are openable, lockable and fixed in place. containers are usually closed.
door is openable and lockable.
object-like is portable.
supporters are fixed in place.
food is edible.
A room has a text called internal name.


The r_0 are rooms.

Understand "laundry place" as r_0.
The internal name of r_0 is "laundry place".
The printed name of r_0 is "-= Laundry Place =-".
The laundry place part 0 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 0 is "You've entered a laundry place. You decide to just list off a complete list of everything you see in the room, because hey, why not?

 You can make out [if c_0 is locked]a locked[else if c_0 is open]an opened[otherwise]a closed[end if]".
The laundry place part 1 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 1 is " cuboid chest.[if c_0 is open and there is something in the c_0] The cuboid chest contains [a list of things in the c_0]. You look around you, at all the containers and supporters, doors and objects, and you think to yourself. Why? Why Textworld?[end if]".
The laundry place part 2 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 2 is "[if c_0 is open and the c_0 contains nothing] Empty! What kind of nightmare TextWorld is this?[end if]".
The laundry place part 3 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 3 is " You make out [if c_1 is locked]a locked[else if c_1 is open]an opened[otherwise]a closed[end if]".
The laundry place part 4 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 4 is " cuboid locker here.[if c_1 is open and there is something in the c_1] The cuboid locker contains [a list of things in the c_1].[end if]".
The laundry place part 5 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 5 is "[if c_1 is open and the c_1 contains nothing] What a letdown! The cuboid locker is empty![end if]".
The laundry place part 6 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 6 is " You see [if c_2 is locked]a locked[else if c_2 is open]an opened[otherwise]a closed[end if]".
The laundry place part 7 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 7 is " box.[if c_2 is open and there is something in the c_2] The box contains [a list of things in the c_2].[end if]".
The laundry place part 8 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 8 is "[if c_2 is open and the c_2 contains nothing] The box is empty! What a waste of a day![end if]".
The laundry place part 9 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 9 is " You scan the room for a type 6 box, and you find a type 6 box.[if c_3 is open and there is something in the c_3] The type 6 box contains [a list of things in the c_3].[end if]".
The laundry place part 10 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 10 is "[if c_3 is open and the c_3 contains nothing] The type 6 box is empty, what a horrible day![end if]".
The laundry place part 11 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 11 is " You see a type 1 locker.[if c_4 is open and there is something in the c_4] The type 1 locker contains [a list of things in the c_4].[end if]".
The laundry place part 12 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 12 is "[if c_4 is open and the c_4 contains nothing] The type 1 locker is empty! What a waste of a day![end if]".
The laundry place part 13 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 13 is " If you haven't noticed it already, there seems to be something there by the wall, it's a type R chest.[if c_5 is open and there is something in the c_5] The type R chest contains [a list of things in the c_5].[end if]".
The laundry place part 14 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 14 is "[if c_5 is open and the c_5 contains nothing] The type R chest is empty! This is the worst thing that could possibly happen, ever![end if]".
The laundry place part 15 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 15 is " If you haven't noticed it already, there seems to be something there by the wall, it's a bench. The bench is usual.[if there is something on the s_0] On the bench you see [a list of things on the s_0].[end if]".
The laundry place part 16 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 16 is "[if there is nothing on the s_0] But the thing hasn't got anything on it. Hm. Oh well[end if]".
The laundry place part 17 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 17 is " You can make out a rack. The rack is typical.[if there is something on the s_1] On the rack you can make out [a list of things on the s_1].[end if]".
The laundry place part 18 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 18 is "[if there is nothing on the s_1] But oh no! there's nothing on this piece of junk.[end if]".
The laundry place part 19 is some text that varies. The laundry place part 19 is "

".
The description of r_0 is "[laundry place part 0][laundry place part 1][laundry place part 2][laundry place part 3][laundry place part 4][laundry place part 5][laundry place part 6][laundry place part 7][laundry place part 8][laundry place part 9][laundry place part 10][laundry place part 11][laundry place part 12][laundry place part 13][laundry place part 14][laundry place part 15][laundry place part 16][laundry place part 17][laundry place part 18][laundry place part 19]".


The c_0 and the c_1 and the c_2 and the c_3 and the c_4 and the c_5 are containers.
The c_0 and the c_1 and the c_2 and the c_3 and the c_4 and the c_5 are privately-named.
The f_0 and the f_1 and the f_2 are foods.
The f_0 and the f_1 and the f_2 are privately-named.
The k_3 and the k_4 and the k_0 and the k_1 and the k_2 and the k_8 are keys.
The k_3 and the k_4 and the k_0 and the k_1 and the k_2 and the k_8 are privately-named.
The o_0 and the o_1 and the o_2 are object-likes.
The o_0 and the o_1 and the o_2 are privately-named.
The r_0 are rooms.
The r_0 are privately-named.
The s_0 and the s_1 are supporters.
The s_0 and the s_1 are privately-named.

